{"description": "Permanently removes named documents from a RAG collection - chunks, retired generations and ledger entries - with a preview mode that reports what would go before anything does.", "displayName": "RAG - Purge Documents.step", "flowMetadata": {"inputPorts": [{"name": "_rgpu_docTable", "displayName": "_rgpu_docTable", "minEntries": 0, "maxEntries": 1, "type": "table", "id": "_rgpu_docTable", "label": "_rgpu_docTable"}], "outputPorts": [{"name": "_rgpu_report", "displayName": "_rgpu_report", "minEntries": 1, "maxEntries": 1, "columnDelta": null, "type": "table"}]}, "metadataVersion": 1, "name": "RAG - Purge Documents.step", "properties": {}, "templates": {"SAS": "/******************************************************************************\n * Copyright \u00a9 2026, SAS Institute Inc., Cary, NC, USA.  All Rights Reserved.\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n *\n * RAG - Purge Documents: permanently remove named documents from a RAG\n * collection - every chunk row, LIVE AND RETIRED - and drop their entries\n * from the ledger so the pipeline forgets them. This is erasure, not the\n * retirement an ingestion run performs: it cannot be undone and an as-of\n * read can no longer reach the removed content. Runs in preview mode by\n * default. Thin shell over rag_core.steps.run_purge - see the About tab.\n ******************************************************************************/\n%macro _rgpu_setup;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgpu_ragProject) %then %global _rgpu_ragProject;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgpu_tablesCaslib) %then %global _rgpu_tablesCaslib;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgpu_tablesCaslib)) EQ 0 %then %let _rgpu_tablesCaslib = casuser;\n%mend _rgpu_setup;\n%_rgpu_setup;\n/* Pipeline-wide state, shared by every RAG step in this session.\n   RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR: 1 (default) stops a SAS Studio Flow at the failing\n   step, which is what an interactive user wants. A SCHEDULED run sets it to\n   0: an aborted session never sends SAS Job Execution its completion\n   handshake, so the job would report running forever and its dead compute\n   server would keep counting against the context's server limit.\n   RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED: set by the step that fails; later steps then skip\n   their work and pass the inventory through, so the flow finishes tidily\n   instead of loading half a corpus. */\n%macro _rag_pipeline_state;\n    %if not %symexist(RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR) %then %do;\n        %global RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR;\n        %let RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR = 1;\n    %end;\n    %if %length(%superq(RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR = 1;\n    %if not %symexist(RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED) %then %global RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED;\n    %if %length(%superq(RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED = 0;\n%mend _rag_pipeline_state;\n%_rag_pipeline_state;\n\n%let _rgpu_viyaHost = %sysfunc(getoption(SERVICESBASEURL));\n%let _rgpu_rc = 1;\n%let _rgpu_state = run;\n%let _rgpu_error = The Python program did not run.;\n%let _rgpu_summary = ;\n%let _rgpu_nreport = 0;\n%let _rgpu_nledger = 0;\n\n%macro _rgpu_guard;\n    %let RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED = 0;\n%mend _rgpu_guard;\n%_rgpu_guard;\n%macro _rgpu_port_default;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgpu_report) %then %global _rgpu_report;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgpu_report)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let _rgpu_report = rgpuout.&_rgpu_ragProject._PURGE_REPORT;\n%mend _rgpu_port_default;\n%_rgpu_port_default;\n/* One CAS session for the whole step: created here, reused by\n   SWAT inside proc python, promote+save done by proc casutil.\n   rgpuout is where the step's OUTPUT TABLE lands by default -\n   the same caslib as the pipeline tables, so a flow leaves its\n   intermediate results next to each other. */\ncas rgpucas uuidmac=_rgpu_casuuid;\n%let _rgpu_cashost = %sysfunc(getoption(CASHOST));\n%let _rgpu_casport = %sysfunc(getoption(CASPORT));\nlibname rgpuout cas caslib=\"&_rgpu_tablesCaslib.\" sessref=rgpucas;\n\n%macro _rgpu_lock;\n    /* %global, not %let: a %let inside a macro makes a LOCAL variable, so the\n       run id would never reach the python block that stamps it on every row */\n    %global _rgpu_lockHeld _rgpu_runId;\n    %local _rgpu_now;\n    %let _rgpu_lockHeld = ;\n    %let _rgpu_now = %sysevalf(%sysfunc(datetime()) - 315619200);\n    %let _rgpu_runId = run-%sysfunc(compress(%sysfunc(putn(&_rgpu_now., 12.))));\n    %if &_rgpu_state. NE run %then %return;\n    %if %sysfunc(exist(rgpuout.&_rgpu_ragProject._LEDGER)) %then %do;\n        data _null_;\n            set rgpuout.&_rgpu_ragProject._LEDGER(where=(doc_id = \"__run_lock__\"));\n            call symputx(\"_rgpu_lockHeld\", mtime, \"G\");\n        run;\n    %end;\n    %if %length(&_rgpu_lockHeld.) GT 0 %then %do;\n        %if %sysevalf(&_rgpu_now. - &_rgpu_lockHeld. < 1800) %then %do;\n            %let _rgpu_state = fail;\n            %let _rgpu_error = another ingestion run holds the lock on this ledger - wait for it to finish, or retry in 30 minutes if it crashed;\n            %return;\n        %end;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"NOTE: RAG - Purge Documents: a stale run lock (held longer than 30 minutes) is ignored\";\n        run;\n    %end;\n    /* take it: append when the ledger exists, otherwise start it */\n    %if %sysfunc(exist(rgpuout.&_rgpu_ragProject._LEDGER)) %then %do;\n        data rgpuout.&_rgpu_ragProject._LEDGER(append=yes);\n            length doc_id varchar(40) source_uri varchar(1024)\n                   source_kind varchar(16) content_hash varchar(64)\n                   mtime varchar(32) status varchar(12)\n                   error_text varchar(512) pipeline_version varchar(32)\n                   config_hash varchar(32) chunk_count 8\n                   run_id varchar(32) updated_at varchar(24);\n            doc_id = \"__run_lock__\";\n            mtime = strip(put(&_rgpu_now., best20.));\n            status = \"lock\";\n            run_id = \"&_rgpu_runId.\";\n            source_uri = \"\"; source_kind = \"\"; content_hash = \"\";\n            error_text = \"\"; pipeline_version = \"\"; config_hash = \"\";\n            chunk_count = 0; updated_at = \"\";\n        run;\n    %end;\n    %else %do;\n        proc casutil sessref=rgpucas\n                     incaslib=\"&_rgpu_tablesCaslib.\"\n                     outcaslib=\"&_rgpu_tablesCaslib.\";\n            droptable casdata=\"&_rgpu_ragProject._LEDGER\" quiet;\n        quit;\n        data rgpuout.&_rgpu_ragProject._LEDGER(promote=yes);\n            length doc_id varchar(40) source_uri varchar(1024)\n                   source_kind varchar(16) content_hash varchar(64)\n                   mtime varchar(32) status varchar(12)\n                   error_text varchar(512) pipeline_version varchar(32)\n                   config_hash varchar(32) chunk_count 8\n                   run_id varchar(32) updated_at varchar(24);\n            doc_id = \"__run_lock__\";\n            mtime = strip(put(&_rgpu_now., best20.));\n            status = \"lock\";\n            run_id = \"&_rgpu_runId.\";\n            source_uri = \"\"; source_kind = \"\"; content_hash = \"\";\n            error_text = \"\"; pipeline_version = \"\"; config_hash = \"\";\n            chunk_count = 0; updated_at = \"\";\n        run;\n    %end;\n    /* a lock that failed to write is not a lock: refuse rather than let a\n       second ingestion interleave unguarded */\n    %let _rgpu_lockHeld = ;\n    data _null_;\n        set rgpuout.&_rgpu_ragProject._LEDGER(where=(doc_id = \"__run_lock__\" and run_id = \"&_rgpu_runId.\"));\n        call symputx(\"_rgpu_lockHeld\", run_id, \"G\");\n    run;\n    %if %length(&_rgpu_lockHeld.) EQ 0 %then %do;\n        %let _rgpu_state = fail;\n        %let _rgpu_error = the run lock could not be written to &_rgpu_tablesCaslib..&_rgpu_ragProject._LEDGER - refusing to ingest unguarded;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgpu_lock;\n%_rgpu_lock;\n%macro _rgpu_export(portvar, file);\n    %if %symexist(&portvar.) %then %do;\n        %if %length(%superq(&&portvar.)) GT 0 %then %do;\n            %if %sysfunc(exist(&&&portvar..)) %then %do;\n                filename _rgpu_io \"%sysfunc(pathname(work))/&file.\";\n                proc json out=_rgpu_io noSASTags;\n                    export &&&portvar..;\n                run; quit;\n                filename _rgpu_io clear;\n            %end;\n        %end;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgpu_export;\n%_rgpu_export(_rgpu_documents, rgpu_documents_in.json);\n\nproc python restart;\nsubmit;\ndef main():\n    import json\n    import os\n    import sys\n    import tempfile\n    import time\n    import traceback\n\n    # nothing to do when the step is only passing the inventory through\n    if str(SAS.symget(\"_rgpu_state\") or \"run\").strip() != \"run\":\n        return\n\n    def sas_safe(text):\n        \"\"\"Strings crossing into SAS.logMessage/SAS.symput are embedded into\n        generated SAS statements - quotes and macro characters corrupt the\n        code stream (verified live). EVERY such string goes through here.\"\"\"\n        cleaned = str(text)\n        for ch in (\"'\", '\"', \"%\", \"&\", \";\"):\n            cleaned = cleaned.replace(ch, \" \")\n        return cleaned\n\n    def M(msg):\n        SAS.logMessage(\"RAGPURGE \" + sas_safe(msg))\n\n    try:\n        import requests\n    except Exception:\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgpu_error\", \"The Python environment of this compute \"\n                                   \"context lacks the requests package - see \"\n                                   \"the RAG administration guide.\")\n        return\n    try:\n        import pandas as pd\n        import swat\n    except Exception:\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgpu_error\", \"The Python environment of this compute \"\n                                   \"context lacks the swat/pandas packages \"\n                                   \"required for the CAS table transport - \"\n                                   \"see the RAG administration guide.\")\n        return\n\n    BASE = str(SAS.symget(\"_rgpu_viyaHost\") or \"\").rstrip(\"/\")\n    TOKEN = os.environ.get(\"SAS_SERVICES_TOKEN\", \"\")\n    AUTH = {\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + TOKEN}\n    VERIFY = os.environ.get(\"SSLCALISTLOC\") or os.environ.get(\"CAS_CLIENT_SSL_CA_LIST\") or True\n    WORKPATH = SAS.workpath if SAS.workpath.endswith(os.sep) else SAS.workpath + os.sep\n\n    P = {name: str(SAS.symget(name) or \"\").strip() for name in [\n        \"_rgpu_backend\",\n        \"_rgpu_collection\",\n        \"_rgpu_storeHost\",\n        \"_rgpu_storePort\",\n        \"_rgpu_storeDb\",\n        \"_rgpu_storeSslmode\",\n        \"_rgpu_storeSsl\",\n        \"_rgpu_mode\",\n        \"_rgpu_documents\",\n        \"_rgpu_credentialDomain\",\n        \"_rgpu_runId\",\n        \"_rgpu_ragProject\",\n        \"_rgpu_tablesCaslib\",\n        \"_rgpu_ragCorePath\",\n    ]}\n\n    def read_rows(filename, missing_message):\n        path = WORKPATH + filename\n        if not os.path.exists(path):\n            raise RuntimeError(missing_message)\n        with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            data = json.load(fh)\n        rows = []\n        for row in data if isinstance(data, list) else []:\n            rows.append({str(k).lower(): v for k, v in row.items()})\n        return rows\n\n    def clean_path(raw):\n        \"\"\"Path-selector values arrive scheme-prefixed (sasserver:/...,\n        sascontent:/...); strip the scheme off.\"\"\"\n        value = str(raw or \"\").strip()\n        for scheme in (\"sascontent:\", \"sasserver:\"):\n            if value.lower().startswith(scheme):\n                return value[len(scheme):]\n        return value\n\n    STARTED = time.time()\n    SUMMARY = []\n\n    def summarize(line):\n        \"\"\"One line of the step's log summary (SAS prints them at the end).\"\"\"\n        SUMMARY.append(str(line))\n\n    def publish_summary(target):\n        elapsed = time.time() - STARTED\n        summarize(f\"elapsed {elapsed:.1f}s\")\n        SAS.symput(target, sas_safe(\" | \".join(SUMMARY))[:1500])\n\n    def write_rows(filename, rows, columns, numeric=()):\n        out = []\n        for row in rows:\n            rec = {}\n            for column in columns:\n                value = row.get(column)\n                if column in numeric:\n                    try:\n                        rec[column] = float(value or 0)\n                    except Exception:\n                        rec[column] = 0.0\n                else:\n                    rec[column] = \"\" if value is None else str(value)\n            out.append(rec)\n        with open(WORKPATH + filename, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            json.dump(out, fh)\n        return len(out)\n\n    try:\n        # ---- CAS: reuse the session the step created in SAS ---------------\n        # (sas-studio-custom-steps: Reuse-CAS-session-from-SWAT)\n        import re as _re\n        os.environ.setdefault(\"CAS_CLIENT_SSL_CA_LIST\",\n                              os.environ.get(\"SSLCALISTLOC\", \"\"))\n        conn = swat.CAS(hostname=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgpu_cashost\") or \"\"),\n                        port=int(float(SAS.symget(\"_rgpu_casport\") or 5570)),\n                        password=TOKEN,\n                        session=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgpu_casuuid\") or \"\"))\n        CASLIB = P[\"_rgpu_tablesCaslib\"] or \"casuser\"\n        if not _re.match(r\"^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,19}$\",\n                         P[\"_rgpu_ragProject\"] or \"\"):\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                \"ragProject must be 1-20 characters (letters, digits, \"\n                \"underscores, starting with a letter) so every \"\n                \"project_suffix table name stays within the 32 characters \"\n                \"SAS Studio displays\")\n\n        def project_table(suffix):\n            return P[\"_rgpu_ragProject\"] + suffix\n\n        def stamp(rows):\n            \"\"\"Every inventory row names its pipeline, so the next step\n            inherits the project and caslib instead of asking again.\"\"\"\n            for row in rows:\n                row[\"rag_project\"] = P[\"_rgpu_ragProject\"]\n                row[\"tables_caslib\"] = CASLIB\n            return rows\n\n        def cas_read(name, required_message=None):\n            \"\"\"Read a pipeline table into lower-cased row dicts; absent\n            table = empty (the pipeline's empty state) unless required.\"\"\"\n            if not conn.table.tableExists(caslib=CASLIB, name=name).exists:\n                if required_message:\n                    raise RuntimeError(required_message)\n                return []\n            frame = conn.CASTable(name, caslib=CASLIB).to_frame()\n            rows = []\n            for record in frame.to_dict(\"records\"):\n                row = {}\n                for key, value in record.items():\n                    row[str(key).lower()] = None if pd.isna(value) else value\n                rows.append(row)\n            return rows\n\n        def label_columns(name, columns):\n            \"\"\"Put the shipped column labels on a CAS table - they survive\n            the promote, so the pipeline tables read without the schema.\"\"\"\n            try:\n                from rag_core.steps import column_labels\n                labels = column_labels(columns)\n                if labels:\n                    conn.table.alterTable(\n                        caslib=CASLIB, name=name,\n                        columns=[{\"name\": column, \"label\": label}\n                                 for column, label in labels.items()])\n            except Exception as exc:\n                M(f\"column labels not applied to {name}: {exc}\")\n\n        def cas_stage(name, rows, columns, numeric=()):\n            \"\"\"Upload the session-scope staging table <name>_S with varchar\n            columns (no 32k limit); the SAS side swaps it into the promoted\n            global table and saves it, so the previous state survives a\n            mid-step failure.\"\"\"\n            if not rows:\n                return 0\n            data = []\n            for row in rows:\n                rec = []\n                for column in columns:\n                    value = row.get(column)\n                    if column in numeric:\n                        try:\n                            rec.append(float(value or 0))\n                        except Exception:\n                            rec.append(0.0)\n                    else:\n                        rec.append(\"\" if value is None else str(value))\n                data.append(rec)\n            frame = pd.DataFrame(data, columns=list(columns))\n            spec = [{\"name\": column,\n                     \"type\": \"double\" if column in numeric else \"varchar\"}\n                    for column in columns]\n            conn.upload_frame(frame,\n                              casout={\"name\": name + \"_S\", \"caslib\": CASLIB,\n                                      \"replace\": True},\n                              importoptions={\"fileType\": \"csv\",\n                                             \"allowEmbeddedNewLines\": True,\n                                             \"vars\": spec})\n            label_columns(name + \"_S\", columns)\n            return len(rows)\n\n        # ---- rag_core bootstrap: download the governed SAS Content folder --\n        def get_json(endpoint, **params):\n            response = requests.get(BASE + endpoint, params=params, headers=AUTH,\n                                    verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 30))\n            response.raise_for_status()\n            return response.json()\n\n        def download_folder(folder_id, local_dir):\n            os.makedirs(local_dir, exist_ok=True)\n            count = 0\n            members = get_json(f\"/folders/folders/{folder_id}/members\", limit=200)\n            for member in members.get(\"items\", []):\n                uri = member.get(\"uri\", \"\")\n                if \"/files/files/\" in uri:\n                    content = requests.get(BASE + uri + \"/content\", headers=AUTH,\n                                           verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 60))\n                    content.raise_for_status()\n                    with open(os.path.join(local_dir, member[\"name\"]), \"wb\") as fh:\n                        fh.write(content.content)\n                    count += 1\n                elif \"/folders/folders/\" in uri:\n                    count += download_folder(uri.rsplit(\"/\", 1)[-1],\n                                             os.path.join(local_dir, member[\"name\"]))\n            return count\n\n        core_path = (clean_path(P[\"_rgpu_ragCorePath\"])\n                     or \"/SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core\")\n        root = requests.get(BASE + \"/folders/folders/@item\",\n                            params={\"path\": core_path}, headers=AUTH,\n                            verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 30))\n        if root.status_code != 200:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"rag_core folder {core_path} not found \"\n                               f\"(HTTP {root.status_code}) - deploy it per the \"\n                               \"administration guide\")\n        staging = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"rag_core_\")\n        n_files = download_folder(root.json()[\"id\"], os.path.join(staging, \"rag_core\"))\n        sys.path.insert(0, staging)\n        import rag_core\n        M(f\"rag_core {rag_core.RAG_CORE_VERSION} bootstrapped ({n_files} files)\")\n\n        from rag_core.adapters import get_adapter\n        from rag_core.credentials import fetch_secrets, store_config_from_secrets\n        from rag_core.steps import (LEDGER_COLUMNS, PURGE_COLUMNS,\n                                    resolve_doc_ids, run_purge)\n\n        missing = [name for name in (\"collection\", \"storeHost\", \"storeDb\")\n                   if not P[\"_rgpu_\" + name]]\n        if missing:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"required parameters missing: \"\n                               + \", \".join(missing))\n\n        # preview is the default and anything but the explicit purge value\n        # keeps it: this step cannot be undone, so the safe branch is the one\n        # a typo lands on\n        dry_run = (P[\"_rgpu_mode\"] or \"preview\") != \"purge\"\n        collection = P[\"_rgpu_collection\"]\n\n        ledger = []\n        for row in cas_read(project_table(\"_LEDGER\"),\n                            \"no ledger table for this RAG project - check \"\n                            \"the project name and caslib\"):\n            ledger.append({column: (\"\" if row.get(column) is None\n                                    else row.get(column))\n                           for column in LEDGER_COLUMNS})\n        own_run_id = P[\"_rgpu_runId\"]\n        real_rows = [r for r in ledger if r.get(\"doc_id\") != \"__run_lock__\"]\n        # own_run_id is set by each step before this block: OUR run's lock is\n        # expected (the first step took it), anyone else's means a concurrent\n        # ingestion is live on this ledger\n        lock_rows = [r for r in ledger\n                     if r.get(\"doc_id\") == \"__run_lock__\"\n                     and str(r.get(\"run_id\") or \"\") != str(own_run_id or \"\")]\n        if lock_rows:\n            try:\n                held_for = time.time() - float(lock_rows[0].get(\"mtime\") or 0)\n            except Exception:\n                held_for = 1e9\n            if held_for < 1800:\n                raise RuntimeError(\"another ingestion run holds the lock on \"\n                                   \"this ledger - wait for it to finish, or \"\n                                   \"retry in 30 minutes if it crashed\")\n            M(\"stale run lock ignored (held longer than 30 minutes)\")\n\n        # the documents to remove: a wired table, a typed list, or both\n        selectors = []\n        listed = WORKPATH + \"rgpu_documents_in.json\"\n        if os.path.exists(listed):\n            for row in read_rows(\"rgpu_documents_in.json\", \"\"):\n                for column in (\"doc_id\", \"source_uri\", \"filename\"):\n                    if row.get(column):\n                        selectors.append(str(row[column]))\n                        break\n        typed = str(P[\"_rgpu_documents\"] or \"\").replace(\";\", \"\\n\")\n        for piece in typed.split(\"\\n\"):\n            if piece.strip():\n                selectors.append(piece.strip())\n        if not selectors:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"name the documents to remove - wire a table \"\n                               \"carrying doc_id or source_uri into this step, \"\n                               \"or list their names in the Documents field\")\n\n        doc_ids, unmatched = resolve_doc_ids(selectors, real_rows)\n        for name in unmatched:\n            M(\"not in the ledger, nothing to remove: \" + name)\n        if not doc_ids:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"none of the named documents are in this \"\n                               \"project's ledger - nothing to remove\")\n\n        domain = P[\"_rgpu_credentialDomain\"] or \"agentic-ai-keys\"\n        secrets = fetch_secrets(BASE, TOKEN, domain, verify=VERIFY)\n        if not secrets:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"no credential resolved from domain \" + domain\n                               + \" for this user - see the Managing \"\n                               \"Credentials administration guide\")\n        backend = P[\"_rgpu_backend\"] or \"pgvector\"\n        sslmode = (P[\"_rgpu_storeSslmode\"] if backend == \"pgvector\"\n                   else P[\"_rgpu_storeSsl\"])\n        adapter = get_adapter(backend)\n        adapter.connect(store_config_from_secrets(\n            secrets, backend, P[\"_rgpu_storeHost\"], P[\"_rgpu_storePort\"],\n            P[\"_rgpu_storeDb\"], sslmode))\n        report, remaining = run_purge(doc_ids, real_rows, adapter, collection,\n                                      dry_run=dry_run, log=M)\n        adapter.close()\n\n        for name in unmatched:\n            report.append({\"doc_id\": \"\", \"source_uri\": name,\n                           \"chunks_removed\": 0, \"ledger_removed\": \"no\",\n                           \"outcome\": \"not found\",\n                           \"error_text\": \"no ledger entry matches this name\"})\n\n        n_report = write_rows(\"rgpu_report_out.json\", report, PURGE_COLUMNS,\n                              numeric=(\"chunks_removed\",))\n        # a preview must leave the ledger exactly as it found it: -1 tells the\n        # swap to keep the promoted table untouched\n        n_ledger = -1 if dry_run else cas_stage(\n            project_table(\"_LEDGER\"), remaining, LEDGER_COLUMNS,\n            numeric=(\"chunk_count\",))\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgpu_nreport\", str(n_report))\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgpu_nledger\", str(n_ledger))\n\n        removed = sum(row[\"chunks_removed\"] for row in report)\n        summarize(\"collection \" + collection + \" on \" + backend)\n        summarize((\"PREVIEW - nothing was changed\" if dry_run\n                   else \"PURGED - this cannot be undone\"))\n        summarize(str(len(doc_ids)) + \" documents named, \"\n                  + str(removed) + \" chunk rows \"\n                  + (\"would be removed\" if dry_run else \"removed\")\n                  + \" (live and retired)\")\n        if unmatched:\n            summarize(str(len(unmatched)) + \" names matched no ledger entry\")\n        if not dry_run:\n            summarize(\"ledger \" + CASLIB + \".\" + project_table(\"_LEDGER\")\n                      + \": \" + str(n_ledger) + \" documents remain\")\n        publish_summary(\"_rgpu_summary\")\n\n        try:\n            conn.close(close_session=False)\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgpu_rc\", \"0\")\n    except Exception as error:\n        error_text = f\"{type(error).__name__}: {error}\"\n        M(\"failed: \" + sas_safe(error_text))\n        print(traceback.format_exc())\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgpu_error\", sas_safe(error_text)[:500])\n\n\nmain()\nendsubmit;\nrun; quit;\nproc python terminate;\nrun; quit;\n\n%macro _rgpu_swap(suffix, count);\n    %if &_rgpu_rc. NE 0 %then %return;\n    %if &count. LT 0 %then %return;\n    proc casutil sessref=rgpucas incaslib=\"&_rgpu_tablesCaslib.\"\n                 outcaslib=\"&_rgpu_tablesCaslib.\";\n        droptable casdata=\"&_rgpu_ragProject.&suffix.\" quiet;\n        %if &count. GT 0 %then %do;\n            promote casdata=\"&_rgpu_ragProject.&suffix._S\"\n                    casout=\"&_rgpu_ragProject.&suffix.\";\n            save casdata=\"&_rgpu_ragProject.&suffix.\"\n                 casout=\"&_rgpu_ragProject.&suffix.\" replace;\n        %end;\n        %else %do;\n            deletesource casdata=\"&_rgpu_ragProject.&suffix..sashdat\" quiet;\n        %end;\n    quit;\n%mend _rgpu_swap;\n%_rgpu_swap(_LEDGER, &_rgpu_nledger.);\n\n%macro _rgpu_emit_report;\n    %if &_rgpu_rc. NE 0 %then %return;\n    %local lib table opts;\n    %let lib = %upcase(%scan(&_rgpu_report., 1, .));\n    %let table = %scan(&_rgpu_report., 2, .);\n    %if &lib. EQ %upcase(rgpuout) %then %do;\n        proc casutil sessref=rgpucas\n                     incaslib=\"&_rgpu_tablesCaslib.\"\n                     outcaslib=\"&_rgpu_tablesCaslib.\";\n            droptable casdata=\"&table.\" quiet;\n        quit;\n        %let opts = (promote=yes);\n    %end;\n    %else %let opts = (compress=yes);\n    %if &_rgpu_nreport. GT 0 %then %do;\n        filename rgpureo \"%sysfunc(pathname(work))/rgpu_report_out.json\";\n        libname rgpurej json fileref=rgpureo;\n        data &_rgpu_report.&opts.;\n            length doc_id $ 40 source_uri $ 1024 ledger_removed $ 8\n                      outcome $ 16 error_text $ 500;\n            label doc_id=\"Document ID\" source_uri=\"Source location\"\n                  chunks_removed=\"Chunk rows removed (live and retired)\"\n                  ledger_removed=\"Ledger entry removed\" outcome=\"Outcome\"\n                  error_text=\"Failure reason\";\n            set rgpurej.root(drop=ordinal_root);\n        run;\n        libname rgpurej clear;\n        filename rgpureo clear;\n    %end;\n    %else %do;\n        data &_rgpu_report.&opts.;\n            length doc_id $ 40 source_uri $ 1024 ledger_removed $ 8\n                      outcome $ 16 error_text $ 500;\n            label doc_id=\"Document ID\" source_uri=\"Source location\"\n                  chunks_removed=\"Chunk rows removed (live and retired)\"\n                  ledger_removed=\"Ledger entry removed\" outcome=\"Outcome\"\n                  error_text=\"Failure reason\";\n            call missing(of _all_);\n            stop;\n        run;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgpu_emit_report;\n%_rgpu_emit_report;\n%macro _rgpu_release;\n    %local failing;\n    %let failing = 0;\n    %if &_rgpu_state. EQ fail %then %let failing = 1;\n    %if &_rgpu_state. EQ run %then %if &_rgpu_rc. NE 0 %then %let failing = 1;\n    %if &failing. EQ 0 %then %return;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgpu_runId) %then %return;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgpu_runId)) EQ 0 %then %return;\n    %if not %sysfunc(exist(rgpuout.&_rgpu_ragProject._LEDGER)) %then %return;\n    data rgpuout.&_rgpu_ragProject._LEDGER_R(replace=yes);\n        set rgpuout.&_rgpu_ragProject._LEDGER(where=(not (doc_id = \"__run_lock__\"\n                                 and run_id = \"&_rgpu_runId.\")));\n    run;\n    proc casutil sessref=rgpucas incaslib=\"&_rgpu_tablesCaslib.\"\n                 outcaslib=\"&_rgpu_tablesCaslib.\";\n        droptable casdata=\"&_rgpu_ragProject._LEDGER\" quiet;\n        promote casdata=\"&_rgpu_ragProject._LEDGER_R\"\n                casout=\"&_rgpu_ragProject._LEDGER\";\n        save casdata=\"&_rgpu_ragProject._LEDGER\"\n             casout=\"&_rgpu_ragProject._LEDGER\" replace;\n    quit;\n    data _null_;\n        putLog \"NOTE: RAG - Purge Documents: the run lock was released so the run can be retried\";\n    run;\n%mend _rgpu_release;\n%_rgpu_release;\n\nlibname rgpuout clear;\ncas rgpucas terminate;\n\n%macro _rgpu_status;\n    %if &_rgpu_state. EQ run %then %if &_rgpu_rc. NE 0 %then\n        %let _rgpu_state = fail;\n    %if &_rgpu_state. EQ skip %then %do;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"NOTE: ----- RAG - Purge Documents: skipped -----\";\n        run;\n        %return;\n    %end;\n    %if &_rgpu_state. EQ fail %then %do;\n        %let RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED = 1;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"ERROR: RAG - Purge Documents failed: %superq(_rgpu_error)\";\n        run;\n        %if &RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR. NE 0 %then %do;\n            data _null_;\n                abort 42;\n            run;\n        %end;\n        %return;\n    %end;\n    data _null_;\n        length part $ 500;\n        putLog \"NOTE: ----- RAG - Purge Documents -----\";\n        do i = 1 to countw(\"%superq(_rgpu_summary)\", \"|\");\n            part = strip(scan(\"%superq(_rgpu_summary)\", i, \"|\"));\n            if part ne \"\" then putLog \"NOTE:   \" part;\n        end;\n    run;\n%mend _rgpu_status;\n%_rgpu_status;"}, "type": "code", "ui": "{\n\t\"showPageContentOnly\": true,\n\t\"pages\": [\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t\"id\": \"pageDefinition\",\n\t\t\t\"type\": \"page\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"Definition\",\n\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgpu_info\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Permanently removes named documents from a RAG collection: every chunk row including RETIRED generations, plus the ledger entries, so the pipeline forgets the documents ever existed. This is not what an ingestion run does - a run retires chunks, which keeps them readable as history and reversible. Purging cannot be undone. Leave the mode on Preview to see what would go before anything does.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgpu_mode\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"radiogroup\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Mode:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"items\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"preview\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Preview only - report what would be removed\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"purge\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Purge - permanently remove the chunks (cannot be undone)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t],\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgpu_ragProject\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"RAG project (names the pipeline's CAS tables):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgpu_collection\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Collection to remove the documents from:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgpu_documents\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Documents (file name, full source path or doc id; separate with semicolons):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"e.g. old-policy.pdf; /docs/superseded.md\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgpu_docTable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"inputtable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"...or a table naming them (doc_id / source_uri column):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgpu_storeHost\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Vector store host:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgpu_storeDb\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Database name:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgpu_sectionAdvanced\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Runtime\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgpu_backend\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"dropdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Vector store:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"items\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"pgvector\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"pgvector (PostgreSQL)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"singlestore\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"SingleStore\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t],\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgpu_storePort\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Vector store port (blank = the backend default: 5432 pgvector, 3306 singlestore):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgpu_storeSslmode\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"dropdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"SSL mode:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"items\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"disable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"disable\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"allow\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"allow\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"prefer\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"prefer\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"require\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"require\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"verify-ca\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"verify-ca\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"verify-full\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"verify-full\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t],\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"$_rgpu_backend\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"=\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"pgvector\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgpu_storeSsl\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"dropdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"TLS:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"items\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"require\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"require (TLS)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"disable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"disable (no TLS)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t],\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"$_rgpu_backend\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"=\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"singlestore\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgpu_tablesCaslib\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Caslib holding the pipeline tables:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgpu_credentialDomain\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Credential domain:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgpu_ragCorePath\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"path\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"SAS Content folder holding rag_core (set by the deployment - not editable here):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"pathtype\": \"folder\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"enabled\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"$_rgpu_ragCorePath\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"=\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"__set_by_deployment__\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgpu_report\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"outputtable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Purge report output:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t]\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t\"id\": \"pageAbout\",\n\t\t\t\"type\": \"page\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"About\",\n\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textAbout\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"RAG - Purge Documents step\\n==========\\n\\nErasure for a RAG collection. Name documents the way you know them - a file name, a full source path or a doc id - and the step resolves them against the ledger, removes every chunk row they own INCLUDING retired generations, and drops their ledger entries so an incremental run does not consider them ingested. The report lists what went, what would have gone in Preview mode, and any name that matched nothing. It takes the same run lock as an ingestion, so it cannot run while a flow or the scheduled job is writing the same ledger.\\n\\nFlow wiring: chain the document INVENTORY through every step - RAG - List Documents \u2192 Extract Text \u2192 Chunk Documents \u2192 Embed Chunks \u2192 Load Vector Store. The bulk data travels beside the flow in promoted CAS tables named <project>_ELEMENTS, <project>_CHUNKS, <project>_EMBEDDED and <project>_LEDGER in the tables caslib (each saved to disk, so state survives server restarts; names stay within 32 characters so they display nicely in SAS Studio). Each step's output table lands in that same caslib as <project>_INV_LIST, _INV_EXTRACT, _INV_CHUNK, _INV_EMBED and <project>_LOAD_REPORT unless you point the output port somewhere else. Give every step the SAME project name and caslib.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionPrereqs\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Pre-requisites\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textPrereqs\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Tested on SAS Viya 2026 (Stable).\\n\\n* The rag_core runtime must be deployed to SAS Content (default: /SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core) with deploy-rag-content.ps1/.sh - keep that folder read-only for regular users.\\n* The compute context's Python needs the requests, swat and pandas packages (swat/pandas carry the pipeline tables to CAS - varchar columns, no 32k limit).\\n* CAS available; the runner needs write access to the tables caslib.\\n* A credential domain (default agentic-ai-keys) holding <BACKEND>_RAG_USER/<BACKEND>_RAG_PW entries.\\n* The RAG project's ledger table must exist in the caslib - the ledger is what maps a file name onto the chunks to remove.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionDocumentation\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Documentation\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textDocumentation\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"PURGING CANNOT BE UNDONE. Retired generations go too, so an as-of read can no longer reach the removed content and a rollback cannot bring it back. If the document still exists at its source, the next ingestion run will add it again - erasure has to happen at the source as well.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionChangelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Changelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textChangelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"* Version: 1.2 (29JUL2026)\\n      - SAS Content document sources; output tables land in the tables caslib; labelled columns; numeric and list-of-values fields; run summary in the log\\n* Version: 1.1 (28JUL2026)\\n      - Pipeline tables move to promoted CAS tables via SWAT (varchar, no 32k limit); automatic embed checkpoint\\n* Version: 1.0 (28JUL2026)\\n      - Initial version\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t]\n\t\t}\n\t],\n\t\"syntaxversion\": \"1.3.0\",\n\t\"values\": {\n\t\t\"_rgpu_ragCorePath\": \"/SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core\",\n\t\t\"_rgpu_ragProject\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgpu_tablesCaslib\": \"casuser\",\n\t\t\"_rgpu_collection\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgpu_documents\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgpu_storeHost\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgpu_storePort\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgpu_storeDb\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgpu_mode\": {\n\t\t\t\"value\": \"preview\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"Preview only - report what would be removed\"\n\t\t},\n\t\t\"_rgpu_backend\": {\n\t\t\t\"value\": \"pgvector\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"pgvector (PostgreSQL)\"\n\t\t},\n\t\t\"_rgpu_storeSslmode\": {\n\t\t\t\"value\": \"prefer\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"prefer\"\n\t\t},\n\t\t\"_rgpu_storeSsl\": {\n\t\t\t\"value\": \"require\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"require (TLS)\"\n\t\t},\n\t\t\"_rgpu_credentialDomain\": \"agentic-ai-keys\"\n\t}\n}"}